<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Bodeok</h1><p class="st-meta">670 CE – 684 CE · capital Geummajeo (Iksan)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived puppet kingdom set up by Silla to house Goguryeo refugees under a Goguryeo prince after the fall of Pyongyang.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/goguryeo">Goguryeo</a> fell in 668, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/silla">Silla</a> backed resistance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>. In 670 it recognised <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anseung">Anseung</a>, a Goguryeo royal, as king of Goguryeo and settled him and his followers at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iksan">Geummajeo</a>, modern Iksan, in former <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/baekje">Baekje</a> territory. In 674 Silla renamed him king of Bodeok.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Bodeok served Silla's purposes during the war against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/later-tang">Tang</a>, giving <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/goguryeo">Goguryeo</a> refugees a figurehead and troops a base. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anseung">Anseung</a> married into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/silla">Silla</a> royal house, and the kingdom sent envoys to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. Its autonomy was limited and it remained under close Silla control.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 683 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anseung">Anseung</a> was summoned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeongju">Gyeongju</a>, given the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/silla">Silla</a> royal surname Kim and settled there. When his kinsman Daemun rebelled in 684, Silla crushed the revolt, abolished the kingdom and dispersed its people.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 670 CE – 684 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Korea and Japan</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:73.03%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>670 CE – 684 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Geummajeo (Iksan)</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Anseung</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/south-korea">South Korea</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Bodeok, Podok, Goguryeo restoration state</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=677&amp;focus=bodeok" aria-label="Bodeok on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7904 857 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Bodeok lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M8115 1035h0M8260 1139h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8224 1113h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M8224 1113h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day South Korea. <a href="/atlas?year=677&amp;focus=bodeok">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
